# Copy to .env.production.local (or set in the Vercel project's
# Environment Variables) before a production/preview build where the
# frontend and backend are on different origins (Vercel + Render).
#
# Leave unset for local dev — the Vite dev server proxies /api/* to the
# local backend (see vite.config.ts), so relative paths already work.
#
# No trailing slash.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com

# --- Hosting modes -------------------------------------------------------
# SAME-ORIGIN (recommended): leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset and run, once the backend host is known,
#     npm run configure:proxy -- https://<backend-host>
# which rewrites web/vercel.json so Vercel forwards /api/* to the backend. The session cookie is then first-party. The backend must still list this frontend's public
# origin in ALLOWED_ORIGINS (the Origin check on POST requests uses it), and RCS_PASSWORD_RESET_LINK_BASE must be this same origin.
# CROSS-ORIGIN: set VITE_API_BASE_URL (above) and ALLOWED_ORIGINS on the backend; the cookie is then third-party and blocked by Safari/Firefox by default, so prefer
# same-origin or custom domains under one registrable domain.
# Optional help links shown in Settings (https only; support may also be mailto:). Unset = the row says no official link is configured yet.
# VITE_SUPPORT_URL=
# VITE_PRIVACY_URL=
# VITE_TERMS_URL=
